# PR Review Prevention — Ship It Right The First Time

Each line below exists because a real core-fe PR shipped without it and a human
reviewer had to catch it. Treat them as part of "done", not as review feedback.

This rule is always loaded, so it stays **short**: one sentence per
non-negotiable, and the owning skill holds the procedure. Do not restate the
detail here — read the skill.

| Non-negotiable | Owner |
| -------------- | ----- |
| **A gate you have not watched fail is not a gate.** Probe both directions, from every layer glob, and wire it into `pr-ci.yml` — `health-check.sh` is local-only. | `guard-authoring` |
| **Never read an exit code through a pipe.** `pnpm lint \| tail -5` reports `tail`'s status; this already produced a false "all passing" here. Capture it or `set -o pipefail`. | `guard-authoring` |
| **Finish the sweep, or scope it to whole units.** Grep the sibling forms, not the list you started with. A half-converted component is a bug; an untouched one is a known gap declared in the PR body. | `pre-pr-sweep` |
| **Deleting a surface means deleting its registrations** — route mount, precache, chunk list, analytics event, store slice, locale keys, test ids, docs. `knip` sees none of those, and a test is not a consumer. | `pre-pr-sweep` |
| **A staleness guard must cover every path.** Extract a helper, route every call site through it, and put the check at the mutation boundary — not in the caller, which cannot protect side effects behind an `await`. | `pre-pr-sweep` |
| **Module-scope `import()` is eager** and defeats the split; use `onceAsync()`. `pnpm build:check` will not catch it. | `bundle-performance` |
| **Regenerate derived artifacts last.** `pnpm sync:check` runs after the final file exists, and again after any new one. | `pre-pr-sweep` |
| **Keep the PR body true to the branch.** Reconcile against `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD`; do not overclaim in the title. | `documentation-maintenance` |

Skills live at `agent-os/skills/<owner>/SKILL.md`. Before opening a PR, run the
full checklist in `pre-pr-sweep`.
